Article 3 (Disqualifications)
(1) A person falling under any of the following shall not be selected as a candidate for an expert commissioner or commissioned as a full-time expert commissioner or appraisal management commissioner: <Amended on October 2, 2014; November 1, 2016; and November 29, 2024.>
1. A person under adult guardianship or limited guardianship;
2. A person declared bankrupt who has not been reinstated;
3. A person for whom five years have not elapsed after completion of execution of a sentence of imprisonment without labor or a heavier punishment, or after a final determination that the person will not be subject to execution of such sentence;
4. A person for whom two years have not elapsed after expiration of the period of suspension of execution of a sentence of imprisonment without labor or a heavier punishment;
5. A person currently within the period of suspension of pronouncement of a sentence of imprisonment without labor or a heavier punishment;
6. A person who has lost or had qualifications suspended by a court judgment or another Act;
7. A person for whom five years have not elapsed since receiving a disciplinary dismissal from public office;
8. A person for whom three years have not elapsed since receiving a disciplinary removal from public office.
(2) Where a candidate for an expert commissioner, full-time expert commissioner or appraisal management commissioner falls under any subparagraph of paragraph (1), the person shall be deleted from the list of candidates for expert commissioners and dismissed from the commission as a full-time expert commissioner or appraisal management commissioner, as applicable. <Amended on November 1, 2016; and November 29, 2024.>
(3) Where a candidate for an expert commissioner, full-time expert commissioner or appraisal management commissioner falls under any of the following, the person may be deleted from the candidate list or dismissed from commission: <Amended on November 1, 2016; October 29, 2020; and November 29, 2024.>
1. Where the person is deemed unable to perform duties because of physical or mental disability;
2. Where the person is deemed to have breached official duties or engaged in other conduct rendering the person unfit to serve as an expert commissioner;
3. Where there are other substantial grounds for considering that the person cannot continue activities as an expert commissioner.
